Project Title : 

Bank Customer Churn Analysis Dashboard

A data analytics project analyzing customer churn patterns in a bank using Power BI to identify high-risk customer segments 
and financial impact.

Project Overview :

Customer churn is a critical challenge in the banking industry because retaining customers is significantly cheaper than 
acquiring new ones.
This project analyzes customer churn patterns using data visualization and business intelligence techniques to help 
management identify :

-churn drivers
-high-risk customers
-financial exposure due to churn
-opportunities to improve customer retention

Business Problem :

The bank observed a significant number of customers closing their accounts, but management lacked insights into:

-Which customers are leaving
-Why they are leaving
-Which segments have the highest churn risk
-The financial impact of customer churn

Without these insights, it becomes difficult to implement effective retention strategies.

Project Objectives :

The objective of this project is to build an interactive Power BI dashboard that helps the bank:

-Measure customer churn rate
-Identify high-risk customer segments
-Analyze churn by demographic and behavioral factors
-Quantify financial impact of customer churn
-Support data-driven decision making

Dataset :

Source: Kaggle

Dataset: Bank Customer Churn Dataset

The dataset contains customer information including:

-Customer ID
-Age
-Geography
-Gender
-Credit Score
-Number of Products
-Account Balance
-Credit Card Ownership
-Active Member Status
-Churn Indicator

Tools & Technologies Used :

-Microsoft Power BI
-DAX (Data Analysis Expressions)
-Data Cleaning
-Data Visualization
-Business Intelligence

Dashboard KPIs :

The dashboard tracks key business metrics including:

-Total Customers
-Churned Customers
-Churn Rate
-Balance at Risk
-Average Credit Score of Churned Customers

These KPIs provide a high-level overview of customer attrition and financial impact.

Key Insights :
1️⃣ High Customer Churn Rate
The analysis shows a 24% churn rate, meaning nearly one in four customers leaves the bank.

2️⃣ Geographic Differences in Churn
Customers in Germany show the highest churn rate, indicating potential regional service or competition issues.

3️⃣ Older Customers Are More Likely to Churn
Customers aged 40+ exhibit higher churn behavior, suggesting the need for targeted retention strategies.

4️⃣ Customers with Fewer Products Are More Likely to Leave
Customers with only one product show significantly higher churn rates.

This indicates low engagement with the bank.

5️⃣ Inactive Customers Are at High Risk
Inactive customers are significantly more likely to churn than active customers.

Customer inactivity can act as an early warning signal for churn risk.

Business Recommendations :

Based on the insights, the following data-driven strategies are recommended:

-Implement customer engagement campaigns for inactive users
-Promote cross-selling to increase product adoption
-Launch targeted retention campaigns in high-churn regions
-Introduce personalized financial products for older customers
-Offer incentives for credit card adoption to improve customer engagement

Project Impact :

This dashboard enables the bank to:

-identify high-risk customer segments
-monitor churn trends
-estimate financial risk from customer attrition
-implement proactive retention strategies

The insights I got from this analysis can significantly help reduce churn and improve customer lifetime value.
